# 16. C and the operating system

C has historically been extremely important for systems programming.

Examples include:

```text
Operating systems
      │
      ├── kernels
      ├── device drivers
      ├── system utilities
      └── command-line tools

Networking
      │
      ├── network stacks
      ├── servers
      └── protocol implementations

Embedded systems
      │
      ├── microcontrollers
      ├── firmware
      └── IoT devices
```

Linux, for example, has a very large C codebase.

