# 18. C vs C++

A common misconception is that C is simply an old version of C++.

They are actually different languages.

A simplified historical relationship is:

```text
C
│
└── C++
      │
      ├── classes
      ├── objects
      ├── inheritance
      ├── templates
      └── exceptions
```

C++ began as an extension of C, but has evolved into a much larger and substantially different language.

---

# 19. C vs Java

Since you're learning Java backend development, this comparison is particularly useful.

| C                           | Java                                   |
| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Compiled to native code     | Compiled to JVM bytecode               |
| Manual memory management    | Garbage collection                     |
| Pointers                    | No general pointer arithmetic          |
| Procedural                  | Primarily object-oriented              |
| `struct`                    | `class`                                |
| Header files                | Packages/classes                       |
| Very low-level control      | Higher abstraction                     |
| Native machine execution    | JVM execution                          |
| No built-in GC              | JVM GC                                 |
| Extremely common in systems | Extremely common in enterprise/backend |

Conceptually:

```text
C:

C source
   ↓
compiler
   ↓
native machine code
   ↓
CPU
```

Java:

```text
Java source
    ↓
javac
    ↓
.class bytecode
    ↓
JVM
    ↓
machine code
    ↓
CPU
```

