# 20. Why learn C today?

Even if your ultimate goal is Java backend development, C is valuable because it teaches you things that higher-level languages hide.

Especially:

### 1. Memory

```text
stack
heap
addresses
pointers
bytes
```

### 2. Compilation

```text
source
 → preprocessing
 → compilation
 → assembly
 → object
 → linking
 → executable
```

### 3. Operating systems

```text
process
thread
memory
file
socket
system call
```

### 4. Data representation

```text
integer
floating point
character
byte
binary
memory layout
```

### 5. Performance

You can understand much better what actually happens underneath:

```text
program
   ↓
instructions
   ↓
CPU
   ↓
memory/cache
```

